Mission wired into main.ts. Two wiring faults found by driving the real frame function (advance) rather than by tests: (1) tickMission never called mission.update, so the hose never armed and a fire could never be doused - 3 sprays left bursts at 4; (2) the ability/hose button's visibility was only written when it changed, so it stayed on screen at spawn since its initial mirrored value was true. Both fixed. Verified by driving frames: spawn hides the button; a synthetic pointerdown on the burning house morphs to car-kit/firetruck.glb and responds; the car within HOSE_RANGE gives state active and reveals the hose; presses take bursts 2,1,0 to complete; the town settles to idle; after a fresh fire the hand traced at frame 599 (9.98s), ran 108 frames (1.8s = TRACE_SECONDS) and made its demo tap at frame 707 (11.78s), leaving the mission active. 333 tests, biome 65 files clean, tsc clean, console empty. Screenshots were unavailable (tab not visible on the desktop), so the flame/smoke picture is verified programmatically, not by eye.
